    "summary": "High‑energy Berkeley with soaring Dark Star → El Paso → Space jam",
    "blurb": "Features a blistering Dark Star > El Paso > Space > Deal sequence, sparkling China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider, and a soulful Stella Blue. Jerry’s wah‑wah leads, Phil’s booming bass and Keith’s jazzy piano drive the high‑energy set.",
    "review": "The August 21, 1972 show at Berkeley Community Theater captures the band in top form, riding the momentum of their Europe ’72 tour while forging new improvisational peaks. The first set rolls through classic road‑trip fare with a tight China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider that glistens thanks to Keith’s piano and Jerry’s fluid phrasing, while Stella Blue offers a dreamy contrast before the band launches into a ferocious Playing In The Band. The second set is where the night truly shines: Dark Star unfurls into an explosive El Paso, segues into a spacious, exploratory Space, and lands with a crisp Deal that feels like a musical exhale. Throughout, Jerry’s scorching wah‑wah guitar runs and impassioned vocals ride atop Phil’s massive bass bombs, while Bill Kreutzmann’s looser, organic drumming lets the jams breathe. The soundboard capture is album‑quality, delivering crystal‑clear separation that makes every nuance of this high‑energy performance shine.",
